</div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float">Listing 7: </span>Mutant difficult to detect in <span id="LST7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Options</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Some mutants in our dataset also proved challenging to detect rather than equivalent. For example, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span> shows a mutant that replaces the return type from a <span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SingletonList</span> to an <span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ArrayList</span>, a change that can only be identified by inspecting the type using the <span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">instanceOf</span> operator. This mutant is hard to detect, but may not be desirable for mutation testing since bugs in return types would be caught by the compiler. On the other hand, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span> shows a mutant that can only be detected if an incorrect <span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">String</span> input is used, containing a double hyphen somewhere within. This appears to be a strong and useful mutant since it can reveal potentially serious bugs in <span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">String</span> manipulation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">
<span id="S4.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_middle" style="width:345.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">
<span id="S4.SS2.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif ltx_font_bold">Summary (<span id="S4.SS2.p6.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">RQ 2</span>)<span id="S4.SS2.p6.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">:</span></span> In total 5.75% of all player-submitted mutants are equivalent, which is 6.94% per CUT on average.</span>
</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">IV-C</span> </span><span id="S4.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">RQ 3: How well do players perform at detecting (non-) equivalent mutants?</span></h3>

